{
  "id": "p4-w26-m4",
  "title": "Constrained decoding masks logits, not meaning",
  "alt": "A hand-drawn whiteboard with a seven-state JSON state machine drawn as a chain from START to DONE with EXPECT_COLON highlighted as the current state, a bar chart of thirty vocabulary logits in which all but three are struck through in red and dropped to a hand-drawn minus-infinity floor while the colon, colon-space and whitespace tokens survive, two panels contrasting guaranteed syntax against unchanged F1 of 0.74, the claim that constrained decoding improves quality crossed out and corrected to parseability, and a grouped bar chart where schema validity climbs from 58.5 to 100 percent while field F1 moves only from 0.61 to 0.74.",
  "width": 1000,
  "height": 874,
  "tier": "T2",
  "week": 26,
